---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, POLICY_UPDATED } from "../../components/site-data";
---
<Base
  title="Terms · Is There a Burn Ban?"
  description="Is There a Burn Ban? summarizes official burn ban sources for information only. Always confirm with the official source before you burn."
  path="/terms/"
>
  <main id="content" class="page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <ol>
        <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
        <li aria-current="page">Terms</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="muted">Updated {POLICY_UPDATED}.</p>

    <h2 id="informational">Informational only</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        State, county, city, tribal and federal authorities set burn bans. We summarize reports, orders and standing rules from the sources we check.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Always confirm with the official source before you burn.</strong> Where available we link the report or order.
        An unconfirmed county can link to an official directory. Cities, fire districts and land managers can have separate rules.
      </li>
      <li>"Unsure" (<code>unknown</code>) means the status is unconfirmed.</li>
      <li>
        Sources can be late, wrong or offline, and we can make mistakes copying them. Alerts can be delayed or not arrive.
        Don't rely on this site or its alerts as your only check.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="warranty">No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site, API, MCP server and alerts are free and provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. To the extent the
      law allows, we aren't liable for losses from using them, including fines, fire damage or missed alerts.
    </p>

    <h2 id="data">Using the data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        When you share a report, name the publisher and include the source or directory link in <code>officialUrl</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Verify the original publisher's terms before republishing source records. See <a href="/data/">the dataset page</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        The API and MCP server need no key. Follow the response's cache headers and keep request rates reasonable. We
        may limit or block traffic that degrades the service, and endpoints can change.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="alerts">Alerts</h2>
    <p>
      Email alerts require confirmation and apply to eligible changes we detect. Alert emails include an unsubscribe link for their subscription.
      You can manage push permissions in your browser. See <a href="/privacy/">privacy</a> for what we store.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms; the date above shows the last change. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
